    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Paul Reynolds are offering for sale this partially completed detached family home in a prime letterkenny location\nSituated on an elevated site in the highly sought-after Lisnennan area, Ard na Coille offers a rare opportunity to create and finish your ideal family home in a desirable residential setting. Located just minutes from Letterkenny Town Centre, this impressive detached property combines generous living space with excellent potential for personalisation.\nExtending to approximately 152 sq.m (1,650 sq.ft), the accommodation has been thoughtfully designed to provide bright, spacious, and practical family living throughout.\nWith welcoming entrance hallway, family room, spaciousliving room opening into a birth kitchen/dining area, utility room and guest wc.\nThere are 4 well proportioned bedrooms on first floor, 2 of which are ensuite and a family bathroom. \nThe property is being sold in a partially completed state and requires final completion, including the installation of a heating system and kitchen units. This presents an excellent opportunity for purchasers to finish the home to their own taste and specification, creating a truly bespoke family residence.\nWith its attractive location, generous accommodation, and outstanding potential, Ard na Coille represents an exceptional opportunity for buyers seeking a quality home in the Letterkenny area.\nDefective block test available for inspection."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.4 x 2.0\nOak staircase leading to first floor with under stair storage area\n\nLiving Room - 5.0 x 3.5\nInset solid fuel burner with timber surround and back boiler to compliment the oil fired heating. Door leading to kitchen/dining area.\n\nKitchen/Dining Area - 6.0 x 4.4\nProvisions in place for installation of kitchen units. Patio door leading to rear of property.\n\nUtility Room - 3.0 x 2.6\n\n\nGuest WC - \nSanitary ware fitted. wc and wash hand basin. Not plastered or tiled.\n\nFamily Room - 4.2 x 3.0\nProvision for fireplace.\n\nLanding - \nHot press - tank to be fitted. Stira stair leading to attic space.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.6 x 3.5\n\n\nWalk in Dressing Room - 2.0 x 1.9\n\n\nEnsuite - \nSanitary ware fitted. wc, wash hand basin and shower. Not plastered or tiled.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.2 x 3.2\n\n\nWalk in wardrobe - \n\n\nEnsuite - \nSanitary ware fitted. wc, wash hand basin and shower. Not plastered or tiled.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.6 x 3.5\n\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.6 x 3.2\n\n\nBathroom - \nSanitary ware fitted. wc, wash hand basin, bath and shower. Not plastered or tiled.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>New Detached Two Storey House</li><li>Originally constructed 2006</li><li>Total floor area approx 152 sq m</li><li>Partially completed internally</li><li>Property ready for installation of kitchen and fireplace.</li><li>Sanitary ware fitted, walls not plastered in bathrooms.</li><li>2nd fix of heating system to be completed, including oil tank, oil boiler, immersion tank & radiators.</li><li>All internal doors, architrave and skirting are oak</li><li>Solid oak staircase leading to first floor</li><li>Bison slab between ground and first floors</li><li>Occupying spacious site</li><li>Natural stone wall on entrance and stone chip driveway.</li><li>Large garden to rear of property</li><li>Mature hedgerow for maximum privacy</li><li>Set in a pleasant residential development within close proximity to town centre & local National Schools</li><li>May qualify for the vacant homes grant.</ul>"
      },
